This is a very good way to know what is glass and what isn't.
Once you have 2+ of a specific color of gem, throw one at a
co-aligned unicorn (requires speed and/or patience).  If the
unicorn "is not interested in your junk" it will drop the thrown
gem and there is no effect on your luck.  But you can then
#name/n that type of gem glass.

Once you know one color of glass, you then know that all
other types of gems of that color are valuable.  Do #name/n
on them, throw them at coaligned unicorns, get luck bonus.

When I pick up a gem I Engrave with it to see if it is hard or
soft.  Then I will #name/n it something like "green soft br 11"
or "red soft lev 3".  The hard ones I might even call them
directly their final type if it's not ambiguous.  Knowing the
level it was first discovered does help in identification - In the
main dungeon but not branches some types aren't generated
above certain depths.



